ctural unknown here |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 base | P0 | E006 (enabled by E004) |\n| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern, Managed/Removed | P0 | E008 |\n| Full resource cleanup when `managementState: Removed` | P0 | E008 (validated by E011) |\n| Upstream-first policy (kagenti/* before opendatahub-io/* midstream) | P0 | E004 (and BRANCH-B-E014 for any OTEL work) |\n| Tech Preview maturity, explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) | P0 | E008 (documented in E012) |\n| Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag | P1 | E010 |\n| OLM/CSV packaging with RELATED_IMAGE_* entries for disconnected installation | P1 | E009 |\n| AuthBridge proxy sidecar image built via Konflux with FIPS compliance | P1 | E007 (enabled by E004) |\n| Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required; arm64 only if no additional effort) | P2 | E006, E007 (as scope/AC — arm64 is explicitly conditional) |\n\nAll 9 HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements. Strategy-level acceptance criteria are\nallocated per epic in the epic files (lifecycle ACs → E008/E011; FIPS check-payload ACs →\nE006/E007; dashboard AC → E010; disconnected AC → E009/E011; image-contract documentation\nMUST → E012).\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Scope-trap / contradiction**: the strategy's In-Scope list (\"Agent registration,\n  discovery, observability wiring, console visibility\") describes the operator's runtime\n  capabilities, while Out-of-Scope and the technical approach explicitly defer runtime\n  behavior to RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589. This decomposition follows the technical approach:\n  productization only (build, packaging, DSC integration, dashboard plumbing). Reviewers\n  should confirm the In-Scope list is stale text.\n- **Open MUST from parent RFE**: the OTEL trace sink MUST (RHAIRFE-7451) is unresolved\n  a