{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1be97c25-ee09-4764-9d6d-67112158f3e6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8402857df99a6305","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-_ao2k5ka/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-E001.md","content":"# Validate upstream kagenti-operator readiness and midstream fork state\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves whether the upstream kagenti-operator is functionally\ncomplete enough to productize at Tech Preview maturity, and whether the midstream forks\nunder opendatahub-io are ready to build from. The outcome determines the scope and\napproach of the downstream platform integration work (the DSC component controller,\nmanifest integration, and packaging), and whether the effort estimate holds at L or\nshifts to XL.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Validate that the upstream `kagenti/kagenti-operator` repository (per architecture\n  context overlay 0014) contains functional implementations of all three controllers:\n  - AgentRuntimeReconciler, including metadata fetch from the workload's\n    `/.well-known/agent-card.json` endpoint via mTLS and storage in\n    `AgentRuntime.Status.Card`\n  - MLflowReconciler\n  - ClientRegistrationController\n- Validate that the AgentRuntime CRD (`agent.kagenti.dev/v1alpha1`) schema is stable\n  enough for Tech Preview (post-productization field changes would require migration).\n- Determine whether the operator requires Keycloak as a runtime dependency (the\n  ClientRegistrationController manages OAuth2 client registration with Keycloak), and\n  whether that controller can be disabled for Tech Preview if it is.\n- Verify the state of the midstream forks: `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` is stated\n  to exist — confirm it is set up and synced with upstream; confirm the status of a\n  kagenti-extensions midstream fork.\n- Produce a gap analysis document: if gaps exist, quantify