X design with UXD for the agent list view, resolving the TP depth\n  decision (tab in an existing project view vs standalone navigation entry).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the dashboard deployed with the feature flag active, when a user navigates to\n  the agent views, the dashboard displays a list of AgentRuntime CRs from the user's\n  accessible namespaces, retrieved via the BFF API proxy.\n- When the kagenti-operator component is `Removed` in DSC, all agent-related UI\n  elements are hidden.\n- The new BFF sidecar runs on an allocated port with no collision with existing\n  Module Federation ports.\n- UX design for the agent list view is finalized and reviewed with UXD, and the TP\n  depth decision (tab vs standalone section) is documented.\n- Go BFF builds with FIPS-compliant settings consistent with the other dashboard BFF\n  sidecars.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P1: Dashboard integration infrastructure — BFF plugin registration and feature flag\n  for agent views (RFE acceptance criterion).\n- Covers strategy acceptance criterion 6 (dashboard displays AgentRuntime list).\n\n## Risks (in-scope)\n\n- BFF sidecar port collision with existing Module Federation ports — mitigated by\n  allocating the next available port and verifying against current assignments\n  (strategy risk table).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":88032,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84864ca943d127bf","agent_id":"a178eccc3072bed73","session_id":"7408e02f-2a40-4c49-b134-f5e8ed6e24cb","uuid":"7deba87e-b310-4e50-b628-0a64df1b8bdb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:09:10.594Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006"}
