migration).\n47\t- Determine whether the operator requires Keycloak as a runtime dependency (the\n48\t  ClientRegistrationController manages OAuth2 client registration with Keycloak), and\n49\t  whether that controller can be disabled for Tech Preview if it is.\n50\t- Verify the state of the midstream forks: `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` is stated\n51\t  to exist — confirm it is set up and synced with upstream; confirm the status of a\n52\t  kagenti-extensions midstream fork.\n53\t- Produce a gap analysis document: if gaps exist, quantify the work (the strategy's\n54\t  threshold is 2 sprints) and identify scope-reduction options for Tech Preview\n55\t  (e.g. defer MLflowReconciler, defer ClientRegistrationController).\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A gap analysis document exists that inventories each of the three controllers and the\n60\t  AgentRuntime CRD against overlay 0014, with a functional/disabled/missing verdict per\n61\t  item.\n62\t- The Keycloak runtime dependency question has a documented answer: required or not for\n63\t  TP, and whether the ClientRegistrationController can be disabled.\n64\t- Midstream fork state (existence, sync status, sync process) is documented for both\n65\t  kagenti-operator and kagenti-extensions.\n66\t- A go/no-go recommendation is produced: proceed at L estimate, or trigger scope\n67\t  reduction / XL escalation with named deferral candidates.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- Enables the P0 HLRs for DSC component integration and Tech Preview maturity by\n72\t  de-risking the assumption that a functional upstream operator exists (strategy\n73\t  assumption flagged \"critical, must validate in sprint 1\").\n74\t- Validates the upstream dependency rows in the strategy's dependency table.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93a87d1d04a08942","agent_id":"aa33879fc1b0e063d","session_id":"7408e02f-2a40-4c49-b134-f5e8ed6e24cb","uuid":"c761b44e-6900-4b72-82cb-e3cf2987e089","timestamp":"2026-10-