tream operator\n49\thas functional gaps, the controller's manifest set and scope are rewritten (deferred\n50\tcontrollers, different manifest content), or the work escalates to XL with a scope\n51\treduction.\n52\t\n53\t## Scope\n54\t\n55\t- Define the `KagentiOperator` component CRD in the\n56\t  `components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` group, following the pattern of\n57\t  `ModelRegistry`, `Trainer`, and other component CRDs, and extend the DSC CR schema\n58\t  with the kagenti component field.\n59\t- Implement the component controller with the standard action pipeline (initialize,\n60\t  releases, kustomize render, deploy, check deployments, garbage collect) and register\n61\t  it in the component registry so the DSC controller manages it.\n62\t- Implement the `managementState` lifecycle: `Managed` deploys the operator with its\n63\t  CRDs, RBAC, and mutating webhook into `redhat-ods-applications` (the operator watches\n64\t  all namespaces for AgentRuntime CRs); `Removed` deletes the controller Deployment,\n65\t  all associated RBAC (ClusterRoles, ClusterRoleBindings, Roles, RoleBindings), the\n66\t  AgentRuntime CRD, the mutating webhook configuration, and namespace-scoped resources\n67\t  in `redhat-ods-applications`.\n68\t- Resolve and document cross-namespace cleanup semantics: what happens to user-created\n69\t  AgentRuntime CRs in other namespaces when the component is disabled (CRD deletion\n70\t  garbage-collects all CRs cluster-wide; the design decision on explicit cross-namespace\n71\t  handling is recorded and tested).\n72\t- Integrate kustomize manifests pulled from the midstream fork at pinned commits into\n73\t  `prefetched-manifests/kagenti-operator/`, with RHOAI-specific overlays for namespace,\n74\t  image references, and RBAC adjustments.\n75\t- Default the component to `Removed` (disabled) so existing clusters are unaffected by\n76\t  upgrade.\n77\t\n78\t## Acceptance Criteria\n79\t\n80\t- Given a fresh RHOAI deployment with the kagenti-operator component set to\n81\t  `managementState: Managed`, when the DSC controller reconciles, the kagenti-operator\n82\t  Deployment is created in `redhat-ods-applications` with the Konflux-built image and\n83\t  becomes Ready.\n84\t- Given the component changed from `Managed` to `Removed`, when the controller\n85\t  reconciles, all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs including\n86\t  `agentruntimes.agent.kagenti.dev`, webhook configuration) are deleted from the\n87\t  cluster.\n88\t- Given the component is `Managed`, when a user creates an AgentRuntime CR referencing\n89\t  an existing Deployment, the operator applies the `kagenti.io/type: agent` label to\n90\t  the target workload (end-to-end validation of the integrated operator).\n91\t- The component defaults to `Removed` in DSC (Tech Preview opt-in) — upgrade of an\n92\t  existing cluster changes nothing.\n93\t- A Konflux-built image digest for kagenti-operator (and the AuthBridge proxy sidecar)\n94\t  is available and wired into the rendered manifests — configuration reference, filled\n95\t  at execution time.\n96\t- The build pipeline for the onboarded component is green (the Konflux pipeline gate\n97\t  for this integration).\n98\t- Cleanup is tested with resources in multiple namespaces; no orphaned AgentRuntime\n99\t  CRs or webhook configurations persist after disable.\n100\t- Rollback/disable safety: setting the component back to `Removed` fully reverts the\n101\t  cluster to its pre-enable state.\n102\t\n103\t## HLR Traceability\n104\t\n105\t- P0: Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR following the standard\n106\t  component controller pattern with `managementState: Managed/Removed` (RFE acceptance\n107\t  criterion).\n108\t- P0: Full resource cleanup when disabled (RFE acceptance criterion).\n109\t- P0: Tech Preview maturity with explicit opt-in, disabled by default in DSC (RFE\n110\t  acceptance criterion).\n111\t- Covers strategy acceptance criteria 1, 2, and 3.\n112\t\n113\t## Risks and Open Questions (in-scope)\n114\t\n115\t- DSC component cleanup leaving orphaned resources — mitigated by an explicit finalizer\n116\t  enumerating owned resources (strategy risk table).\n117\t- kagenti-operator running alongside other platform operators in\n118\t  `redhat-ods-applications` without RBAC conflicts — validated as part of this work\n119\t  (strategy assumption).\n120\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93a87d1d04a08942","agent_id":"aa33879fc1b0e063d","session_id":"7408e02f-2a40-4c49-b134-f5e8ed6e24cb","uuid":"1c3d4862-3a25-4fdf-8a60-ca5301fc5125","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:16:14.064Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-89ce630f4282e6b6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
