changes |\n129\t| E006 ↛ E008 | Rule 10 (konflux-onboarding ∥ general implementation) | No edge in either direction; coupling enforced by the \"build pipeline green\" and \"Konflux-built image digest available\" ACs on E008 |\n130\t| E007 ↛ E008 | Rule 10 | Same as above; the AuthBridge image digest is an AC gate on E008, not a DAG dependency |\n131\t| E008 → E009 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact: CRD/RBAC) | The CSV declares the KagentiOperator CRD and the component controller's RBAC, which E008 produces |\n132\t| E008 → E010 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact: DSC schema / CRD) | The dashboard feature flag is gated by the kagenti component state in the DSC CR (schema extension produced by E008) and the BFF reads AgentRuntime CRs deployed through it |\n133\t| E008 → E011 | Rule 12/13 analog | The E2E suite exercises the deployed component lifecycle |\n134\t| E009 → E011 | Rule 13 analog | Disconnected-install validation requires the CSV with RELATED_IMAGE entries |\n135\t| E006/E007 ↛ E009 | Rule 13 (image digest = configuration reference) | SHA256-pinned digests are filled in at execution time; E009 gets a \"pinned image digests available\" AC, NOT a dependency on the Konflux epics |\n136\t| All Implementations → E012 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Documentation describes what was built; blocked by all main-plan Implementation epics (E004–E011) |\n137\t| E002 → BRANCH-B-E013 | Rule 3 + conditional branch | Variant-set outcome (≤3 bounded outcomes) determines whether additional Konflux components exist. Branch A (proxy-only, the strategy's committed TP minimum) needs no additional epics |\n138\t| E003 → BRANCH-B-E014 | Rule 3 + conditional branch | OTEL scope outcome (in/out of TP scope) determines whether an integration epic exists. Branch A (out of scope, remains with the parent RFE/ARC) needs no additional epics |\n139\t| E004 → BRANCH-B-E013/E014 | Rule 6 | Both branch epics build in the midstream forks |\n140\t\n141\t## Unknowns Handling (Step 3 scan