{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2e7004a026ee5a0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E011\n3\ttitle: E2E test plan and suite for kagenti component lifecycle\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: QE\n6\tteam: QE\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E008\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E009\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 0\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 4\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# E2E test plan and suite for kagenti component lifecycle\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tCreate the QE test plan and E2E test suite for the kagenti-operator component:\n36\tcomponent lifecycle (Managed/Removed with full cleanup), agent registration flow,\n37\twebhook ordering interactions, and disconnected-installation validation. This epic\n38\tvalidates the platform integration and packaging work and is required for Tech Preview\n39\treadiness.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Test plan covering component lifecycle, agent onboarding, and disconnected\n44\t  installation for the kagenti-operator component.\n45\t- E2E tests for the Managed/Removed lifecycle: deployment creation in\n46\t  `redhat-ods-applications`, full resource cleanup on disable (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs,\n47\t  webhook configuration), including resources in multiple namespaces.\n48\t- E2E test for the agent registration flow: creating an AgentRuntime CR referencing an\n49\t  existing Deployment results in the `kagenti.io/type: agent` label on the target\n50\t  workload.\n51\t- E2E tests for AuthBridge mutating-webhook ordering alongside other platform mutating\n52\t  webhooks (HardwareProfile, connection injection), exercising the\n53\t  `reinvocationPolicy: IfNeeded` behavior.\n54\t- Disconnected-installation validation using image mirroring through the\n55\t  RELATED_IMAGE entries.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A reviewed test plan exists covering the scope above.\n60\t- The E2E suite runs green against a cluster with the kagenti-operator component\n61\t  enabled, using Konflux-built operator and AuthBridge proxy images (image digests as\n62\t  configuration inputs, not build outputs of this epic).\n63\t- Lifecycle tests demonstrate no orphaned AgentRuntime CRs or webhook configurations\n64\t  after the component is disabled, including multi-namespace scenarios.\n65\t- Webhook ordering tests demonstrate no pod-creation failures or unexpected sidecar\n66\t  behavior when the kagenti webhook runs alongside other platform mutating webhooks.\n67\t- Disconnected validation demonstrates the operator running with images resolved from\n68\t  a mirrored registry.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- Validates the P0 HLRs for DSC enable/disable and full cleanup on `Removed` (RFE\n73\t  acceptance criteria) and the P0 Tech Preview opt-in behavior.\n74\t- Supports the P1 OLM/CSV disconnected-installation HLR through validation.\n75\t- Covers strategy acceptance criteria 2, 3, and 7 from a validation perspective.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f9c3a8967f78be5","agent_id":"ae9bc348bba6a12a4","session_id":"7408e02f-2a40-4c49-b134-f5e8ed6e24cb","uuid":"a9b8b424-eda9-4806-8229-7a8d8bdbad95","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:24:02.654Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2e7004a026ee5a0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
