{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2148b24f7250bcf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n3\tepic_count: 13\n4\tcritical_path_length: 6\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: true\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8006 ([TP] Productize & Downstream the Agent Operator)\n11\t\n12\tTriage: none. The strategy is L-sized (6–9 sprints), spans four components\n13\t(kagenti-operator, kagenti-extensions/AuthBridge, rhods-operator, odh-dashboard) and four\n14\timplementation teams (Kagenti, Platform / ODH Operator, Dashboard, plus QE and Docs\n15\tinvolvement). Neither below-threshold nor docs-only; full decomposition follows.\n16\t\n17\tStaff Engineer Input: the section contains only template placeholder text — no overrides\n18\tto log.\n19\t\n20\t## Component Mapping Notes\n21\t\n22\tCanonical component names (from `.context/rhai-components.txt`) do not include kagenti\n23\trepositories. Non-obvious mappings applied:\n24\t\n25\t| Strategy component | Canonical component used | Rationale |\n26\t| --- | --- | --- |\n27\t| kagenti-operator | Agentic | No kagenti component in the canonical list; Agentic is the closest parent-level component for kagenti agent-operator work |\n28\t| kagenti-extensions (AuthBridge) | Agentic | Same sub-system, same owning team (Kagenti); separate epics because they live in different repositories |\n29\t| rhods-operator | AI Core Platform | rhods-operator is the RHOAI platform operator; AI Core Platform is the closest canonical platform-operator component |\n30\t| odh-dashboard | AI Core Dashboard | Direct match for the dashboard console |\n31\t| OTEL trace sink (open scope item) | Model and Agent Observability | Closest canonical component for agent observability work |\n32\t\n33\tQE and Docs deliverables (the E2E validation epic and the installation/image-contract\n34\tdocumentation epic) target the kagenti-operator component being productized, so those\n35\tepics use the canonical component Agentic rather than a team-name component; the\n36\tperforming teams (QE, Docs) remain in the `team` field.\n37\t\n38\tNew-component detection: kagenti-operator and kagenti-extensions have no architecture\n39\tcontext files (not \"in platform\"), so the Rule 20 onboarding chain applies\n40\t(repo-onboarding + license-validation parallel → konflux-onboarding → general\n41\timplementation). The midstream fork `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` is stated to exist\n42\tbut its sync state needs validation; the kagenti-extensions fork status is unstated, so\n43\trepo-onboarding covers establishing/syncing both forks.\n44\t\n45\t## Epic List\n46\t\n47\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n48\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n49\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 | Validate upstream kagenti-operator readiness and midstream fork state | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n50\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 | Determine AuthBridge sidecar variant set for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n51\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E003 | Resolve OTEL trace sink scope for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n52\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E004 | Establish and sync opendatahub-io midstream forks for kagenti repos | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n53\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E005 | License validation for kagenti-operator and kagenti-extensions transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P0 |\n54\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E006 | Konflux build onboarding for kagenti-operator image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n55\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E007 | Konflux build onboarding for AuthBridge proxy sidecar image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n56\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E008 | KagentiOperator component CRD, DSC schema, and registry registration | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n57\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E015 | KagentiOperator component controller pipeli