or this strategy — runtime discovery behavior is RHAIRFE-7587/7588; the documentation epic documents the current upstream contract (`/.well-known/agent-card.json`) |\n189\t| Onboarding CR interaction with OpenShell Sandbox CR | Out of scope — runtime behavior tracked by RHAIRFE-7587; OpenShell exists in architecture context and is unaffected by productization |\n190\t| Konflux pipeline capacity (needs submission) | Process risk on E006/E007 (human gate), not an unknown that changes epic structure; escalation path captured in the strategy risk table |\n191\t| AgentRuntime CRD schema stability for TP | Validated as part of E001; schema changes after productization are migration work, not a structural unknown here |\n192\t\n193\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n194\t\n195\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n196\t| --- | --- | --- |\n197\t| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 base | P0 | E006 (enabled by E004) |\n198\t| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern, Managed/Removed | P0 | E008 (CRD/schema/registry definition), E015 (lifecycle enforcement) |\n199\t| Full resource cleanup when `managementState: Removed` | P0 | E015 (validated by E011) |\n200\t| Upstream-first policy (kagenti/* before opendatahub-io/* midstream) | P0 | E004 (and BRANCH-B-E014 for any OTEL work) |\n201\t| Tech Preview maturity, explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) | P0 | E008 (schema default), E015 (enforced lifecycle), documented in E012 |\n202\t| Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag | P1 | E010 |\n203\t| OLM/CSV packaging with RELATED_IMAGE_* entries for disconnected installation | P1 | E009 (extended to additional variants by BRANCH-B-E016) |\n204\t| AuthBridge proxy sidecar image built via Konflux with FIPS compliance | P1 | E007 (enabled by E004) |\n205\t| Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required; arm64 only if no additional effort) | P2 | E006, E007 (as scope/AC — arm64