ption (strategy frontmatter `priority: Critical` → P0) even though it is last in\n237\t  the DAG. This is rule-mandated, not a planning error.\n238\t- **Data quality**: the strategy's third acceptance criterion references CRD\n239\t  `agentrimes.agent.kagenti.dev` — a typo for `agentruntimes.agent.kagenti.dev`; epics\n240\t  use the correct name.\n241\t- **Process gates pending**: Architecture Review, Build Onboarding, License Validation,\n242\t  UXD and Documentation support are all \"Pending human review\" in the strategy — these\n243\t  are captured as human-gate signals on the relevant epics rather than DAG edges.\n244\t\n245\t## Tiered Delivery\n246\t\n247\tTier 1 (independent partial value, proceed immediately):\n248\t- E004 (midstream forks), E005 (license validation), E006/E007 (Konflux onboarding —\n249\t  the critical-path lead-time item the strategy says to submit immediately), and\n250\t  E001–E003 (investigations). None of this is blocked by upstream functional readiness.\n251\t\n252\tTier 2 (gated):\n253\t- E008 (component definition) is gated by E001 (upstream readiness) and E005\n254\t  (licenses); E015 (controller pipeline and lifecycle) follows E008 and the same gates;\n255\t  E009/E010/E011 follow; E012 (docs) is last.\n256\t- Conditional branches: BRANCH-B-E013 (Konflux onboarding, Kagenti) and BRANCH-B-E016\n257\t  (CSV RELATED_IMAGE entries, Platform) activate only if the E002 outcome selects\n258\t  additional variants for TP; BRANCH-B-E014 (upstream-first OTEL integration, Kagenti)\n259\t  and BRANCH-B-E017 (DSC configuration surface, Platform) activate only if the E003\n260\t  outcome pulls the parent-RFE MUST into this strategy's TP scope. Branch A outcomes\n261\t  (proxy-only; OTEL stays with the parent RFE) require no additional epics — the main\n262\t  plan already delivers the strategy's committed TP scope.\n263\t\n264\t## Revision Notes (post-review)\n265\t\n266\tChanges applied in response to the adversarial review\n267\t(`artifacts/epic-reviews/RHAISTRAT-8006-decomp-review.md`):\n268\t\n269\t- **E008 split (oversized epic)**: the component controller epic — priced at 2–3\n270\t  sprints by the strategy's own estimate — was split along the reviewer-suggested seam\n271\t  into E008 (KagentiOperator CRD, DSC schema, registry registration) and E015\n272\t  (controller pipeline, kustomize manifest integration, Managed/Removed lifecycle and\n273\t  garbage collection). Downstream dependencies were redistributed: E009 and E010 depend\n274\t  on both halves; E011 and the docs chain follow E015; the midstream-fork edge (E004)\n275\t  moved to E015, which owns the manifest integration.\n276\t- **Missing branch DAG edges (critical)**: the rendered-manifest artifact edge to the\n277\t  OTEL branch epic is now E015 → BRANCH-B-E014 (the manifest integration was E008's\n278\t  artifact before the split), and the CSV extension-point edge is E009 → BRANCH-B-E016.\n279\t- **Branch epic team/component boundaries**: the CSV RELATED_IMAGE updates were moved\n280\t  out of the Kagenti konflux epic (BRANCH-B-E013) into the new Platform / ODH\n281\t  Operator conditional epic BRANCH-B-E016; the DSC component configuration surface was\n282\t  moved out of the Kagenti OTEL epic (BRANCH-B-E014) into the new Platform / ODH\n283\t  Operator conditional epic BRANCH-B-E017. BRANCH-B-E013/E014 keep only Kagenti-owned\n284\t  work (variant image builds; upstream-first integration and midstream pull).\n285\t- **Component fields**: E011 and E012 now use the canonical component Agentic instead\n286\t  of the team names QE / Documentation.\n287\t- **Explicit deferral**: the COULD-level acceptance criterion (auto-registration of\n288\t  sandboxed agents) is recorded as deferred to RHAIRFE-7587 (see Deferred strategy\n289\t  items above).\n290\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f648cd401ef5cc9","agent_id":"af9f81e901d4d4be6","session_id":"7408e02f-2a40-4c49-b134-f5e8ed6e24cb","uuid":"649b6f27-3eb8-4ac6-a17c-ee765ad08af4","ti