{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e7153053847fe7e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate upstream kagenti-operator readiness and midstream fork state\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Agentic\n6\tteam: Kagenti\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate upstream kagenti-operator readiness and midstream fork state\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves whether the upstream kagenti-operator is functionally\n30\tcomplete enough to productize at Tech Preview maturity, and whether the midstream forks\n31\tunder opendatahub-io are ready to build from. The outcome determines the scope and\n32\tapproach of the downstream platform integration work (the DSC component controller,\n33\tmanifest integration, and packaging), and whether the effort estimate holds at L or\n34\tshifts to XL.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Validate that the upstream `kagenti/kagenti-operator` repository (per architecture\n39\t  context overlay 0014) contains functional implementations of all three controllers:\n40\t  - AgentRuntimeReconciler, including metadata fetch from the workload's\n41\t    `/.well-known/agent-card.json` endpoint via mTLS and storage in\n42\t    `AgentRuntime.Status.Card`\n43\t  - MLflowReconciler\n44\t  - ClientRegistrationController\n45\t- Validate that the AgentRuntime CRD (`agent.kagenti.dev/v1alpha1`) schema is stable\n46\t  enough for Tech Preview (post-productization field changes would require migration).\n47\t- Determine whether the operator requires Keycloak as a runtime dependency (the\n48\t  ClientRegistrationController manages OAuth2 client registration with Keycloak), and\n49\t  whether that controller can be disabled for Tech Preview if it is.\n50\t- Verify the state of the midstream forks: `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` is stated\n51\t  to exist — confirm it is set up and synced with upstream; confirm the status of a\n52\t  kagenti-extensions midstream fork.\n53\t- Produce a gap analysis document: if gaps exist, quantify the work (the strategy's\n54\t  threshold is 2 sprints) and identify scope-reduction options for Tech Preview\n55\t  (e.g. defer MLflowReconciler, defer ClientRegistrationController).\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A gap analysis document exists that inventories each of the three controllers and the\n60\t  AgentRuntime CRD against overlay 0014, with a functional/disabled/missing verdict per\n61\t  item.\n62\t- The Keycloak runtime dependency question has a documented answer: required or not for\n63\t  TP, and whether the ClientRegistrationController can be disabled.\n64\t- Midstream fork state (existence, sync status, sync process) is documented for both\n65\t  kagenti-operator and kagenti-extensions.\n66\t- A go/no-go recommendation is produced: proceed at L estimate, or trigger scope\n67\t  reduction / XL escalation with named deferral candidates.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- Enables the P0 HLRs for DSC component integration and Tech Preview maturity by\n72\t  de-risking the assumption that a functional upstream operator exists (strategy\n73\t  assumption flagged \"critical, must validate in sprint 1\").\n74\t- Validates the upstream dependency rows in the strategy's dependency table.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f648cd401ef5cc9","agent_id":"af9f81e901d4d4be6","session_id":"7408e02f-2a40-4c49-b134-f5e8ed6e24cb","uuid":"c68e0763-440f-49c5-bf2d-ad3a0610e415","timestamp":"2026-10-