{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b215b74d586d8003","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E002\n3\ttitle: Determine AuthBridge sidecar variant set for Tech Preview\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Agentic\n6\tteam: Kagenti\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Determine AuthBridge sidecar variant set for Tech Preview\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation decides which AuthBridge sidecar image variants ship in Tech\n30\tPreview. Upstream kagenti-extensions provides three variants — `authbridge-proxy` (full\n31\tproxy, default mode), `authbridge-envoy` (Envoy ext_proc mode), and `authbridge-lite`\n32\t(auth-only) — and each variant requires its own Konflux component. The committed TP\n33\tminimum is `authbridge-proxy`; whether the other two variants are needed for this\n34\trelease determines whether additional build-onboarding work exists.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Confirm with product management and the Kagenti team whether `authbridge-envoy` and\n39\t  `authbridge-lite` are required for this release or can ship in a later release.\n40\t- Document the functional consequences of each outcome: which modes TP customers can\n41\t  use, and what the CSV must declare.\n42\t- Record the decision and the rationale, including any customer commitments that\n43\t  require a specific variant.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- A decision document names the exact variant set for Tech Preview (proxy-only, or\n48\t  proxy plus named additional variants).\n49\t- If additional variants are selected, the outcome triggers the conditional\n50\t  build-onboarding work for those variants; if proxy-only, that work is confirmed as\n51\t  deferred to a later release.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- Directly qualifies the P1 HLR \"AuthBridge proxy sidecar image built via Konflux with\n56\t  FIPS compliance\": the proxy variant is committed regardless; this investigation\n57\t  determines whether additional variant onboarding epics exist.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f648cd401ef5cc9","agent_id":"af9f81e901d4d4be6","session_id":"7408e02f-2a40-4c49-b134-f5e8ed6e24cb","uuid":"bc3146e3-7bba-484d-8adc-03670918089c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:43:36.613Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b215b74d586d8003","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
