{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cd051496000f476","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E008\n3\ttitle: KagentiOperator component CRD, DSC schema, and registry registration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: Platform / ODH Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E005\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the upstream readiness investigation finds functional gaps,\n16\t    the component definition (CRD surface, DSC schema, manifest set) and the controller\n17\t    scope are rewritten (defer MLflowReconciler / ClientRegistrationController per\n18\t    the TP scope-reduction options) or the effort escalates to XL with renegotiated\n19\t    TP scope.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: 0\n27\t  human_process_gates: -1\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\timplementation_type: null\n33\tinvestigation_signals: null\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# KagentiOperator component CRD, DSC schema, and registry registration\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tDefine the KagentiOperator component in rhods-operator: the component CRD in the\n42\t`components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` group, the DataScienceCluster CR schema\n43\textension carrying the kagenti component field (defaulting to `Removed` for Tech\n44\tPreview opt-in), and the component registry registration that the DSC controller\n45\titerates. This is the definition half of the component controller work, split from the\n46\tcontroller pipeline and lifecycle epic because the strategy prices the combined work\n47\t(CRD definition, kustomize manifest integration, garbage-collection logic, DSC schema\n48\textension) at 2–3 sprints — above the ~2-week epic guideline. The action pipeline,\n49\tmanifest integration, and Managed/Removed lifecycle are delivered by the follow-on\n50\tcontroller-pipeline epic.\n51\t\n52\tThis epic is gated on the upstream readiness investigation: if the upstream operator\n53\thas functional gaps, the component's scope is rewritten (deferred controllers change\n54\tthe CRD/RBAC surface and manifest content) or the work escalates to XL with a scope\n55\treduction.\n56\t\n57\t## Scope\n58\t\n59\t- Define the `KagentiOperator` component CRD in the\n60\t  `components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` group, following the pattern of\n61\t  `ModelRegistry`, `Trainer`, `FeastOperator`, and the other component CRDs.\n62\t- Extend the DataScienceCluster CR schema with the kagenti component field,\n63\t  defaulting to `Removed` (Tech Preview opt-in) so existing clusters are unaffected\n64\t  by upgrade.\n65\t- Register the component in the rhods-operator component registry\n66\t  (`internal/controller/components/registry/`) so the DSC controller manages it, wired\n67\t  to the controller pipeline delivered by the follow-on controller work.\n68\t\n69\t## Acceptance Criteria\n70\t\n71\t- The `KagentiOperator` CRD is defined in the\n72\t  `components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` group following the existing component\n73\t  CRD pattern, and the DSC CR schema carries the kagenti component field.\n74\t- The component defaults to `Removed` in DSC (Tech Preview opt-in) — upgrade of an\n75\t  existing cluster changes nothing.\n76\t- The component is registered in the component registry and recognized by the DSC\n77\t  controller's component iteration.\n78\t- The CRD and DSC schema changes merge with unit tests covering schema validation and\n79\t  the `Removed` defaulting.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- P0: Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR following the standard\n84\t  component controller pattern — CRD/schema/registry definition half (RFE acceptance\n85\t  criterion).\n86\t- P0: Tech Preview maturity with explicit opt-in, disabled by default in DSC —\n87\t  schema-level default (RFE acceptance criterion).\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f648cd401ef5cc9","agent_id":"af9f81e901d4d4be6","session_id":"7408e02f-2a40-4c49-b134-f5e8ed6e24cb","uuid":"28577264-cc6e-463e-b9d4-c753a4d49843","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:43:50.249Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cd051496000f476","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
