{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b85709704de0cfc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E010\n3\ttitle: Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E008\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E015\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 0\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: -1\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 3\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tRegister a kagenti dashboard plugin in the odh-dashboard Module Federation\n36\tarchitecture: a new Go BFF container that proxies Kubernetes API requests for\n37\tAgentRuntime CR management, plus a feature flag that hides all agent-related UI when\n38\tthe kagenti-operator component is disabled in DSC. For Tech Preview the integration\n39\tprovides read-only agent visibility: a list of AgentRuntime CRs with status and links\n40\tto workload details. Full agent management UI is out of scope.\n41\t\n42\tThis epic builds against the DSC schema extension and the AgentRuntime CR integration\n43\tdelivered by the platform component work, so it follows that work.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Add a `disableKagenti` feature flag (or equivalent) to the `OdhDashboardConfig` CR,\n48\t  gated by the DSC component state: when the kagenti-operator component is `Removed`\n49\t  in DSC, the dashboard hides all agent-related UI elements.\n50\t- Implement a new Go BFF container following the pattern of `gen-ai`, `maas-ui`, and\n51\t  the other federated modules; it runs as a sidecar container in the dashboard pod on\n52\t  a dedicated port allocated from the next available value in the documented port\n53\t  range (existing assignments include 8043 model-registry, 8143 gen-ai, 8243 maas,\n54\t  8343 mlflow, 8443 eval-hub, 8543 automl, 8643 autorag).\n55\t- Implement Module Federation registration for the agent views (frontend remote plus\n56\t  BFF route prefix).\n57\t- Implement the Tech Preview agent list view: list AgentRuntime CRs from the user's\n58\t  accessible namespaces, show status, link to workload details.\n59\t- Finalize the UX design with UXD for the agent list view, resolving the TP depth\n60\t  decision (tab in an existing project view vs standalone navigation entry).\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- Given the dashboard deployed with the feature flag active, when a user navigates to\n65\t  the agent views, the dashboard displays a list of AgentRuntime CRs from the user's\n66\t  accessible namespaces, retrieved via the BFF API proxy.\n67\t- When the kagenti-operator component is `Removed` in DSC, all agent-related UI\n68\t  elements are hidden.\n69\t- The new BFF sidecar runs on an allocated port with no collision with existing\n70\t  Module Federation ports.\n71\t- UX design for the agent list view is finalized and reviewed with UXD, and the TP\n72\t  depth decision (tab vs standalone section) is documented.\n73\t- Go BFF builds with FIPS-compliant settings consistent with the other dashboard BFF\n74\t  sidecars.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- P1: Dashboard integration infrastructure — BFF plugin registration and feature flag\n79\t  for agent views (RFE acceptance criterion).\n80\t- Covers strategy acceptance criterion 6 (dashboard displays AgentRuntime list).\n81\t\n82\t## Risks (in-scope)\n83\t\n84\t- BFF sidecar port collision with existing Module Federation ports — mitigated by\n85\t  allocating the next available port and verifying against current assignments\n86\t  (strategy risk table).\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f648cd401ef5cc9","agent_id":"af9f81e901d4d4be6","session_id":"7408e02f-2a40-4c49-b134-f5e8ed6e24cb","uuid":"454c7435-7bea-4b29-8d74-49a547814196","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:43:52.475Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b85709704de0cfc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
