{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-869b0a989dd1b30e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E015\n3\ttitle: KagentiOperator component controller pipeline and lifecycle\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: Platform / ODH Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E004\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E005\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E008\n14\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: rewrite\n17\t  fallback_approach: If the upstream readiness investigation finds functional gaps,\n18\t    the controller manifest set and scope are rewritten (defer MLflowReconciler /\n19\t    ClientRegistrationController per the TP scope-reduction options) or the effort\n20\t    escalates to XL with renegotiated TP scope.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: -1\n27\t  external_dependency: 0\n28\t  human_process_gates: -1\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 4\n33\timplementation_type: null\n34\tinvestigation_signals: null\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\tbranch: null\n37\t---\n38\t# KagentiOperator component controller pipeline and lifecycle\n39\t\n40\t## Description\n41\t\n42\tImplement the KagentiOperator component controller in rhods-operator behind the CRD,\n43\tDSC schema, and registry registration delivered by the component definition work: the\n44\tstandard action pipeline (initialize, releases, kustomize render, deploy, check\n45\tdeployments, garbage collect), the kustomize manifest integration from the midstream\n46\tfork, and the full Managed/Removed lifecycle with garbage collection. This is the\n47\tsecond half of the component controller work, split from the component definition epic\n48\tbecause the strategy prices the combined work at 2–3 sprints — above the ~2-week epic\n49\tguideline.\n50\t\n51\tThis epic is gated on the upstream readiness investigation: if the upstream operator\n52\thas functional gaps, the controller's manifest set and scope are rewritten (deferred\n53\tcontrollers, different manifest content), or the work escalates to XL with a scope\n54\treduction.\n55\t\n56\t## Scope\n57\t\n58\t- Implement the component controller with the standard action pipeline (initialize,\n59\t  releases, kustomize render, deploy, check deployments, garbage collect), wired to\n60\t  the component registry registration.\n61\t- Implement the `managementState` lifecycle: `Managed` deploys the operator with its\n62\t  CRDs, RBAC, and mutating webhook into `redhat-ods-applications` (the operator watches\n63\t  all namespaces for AgentRuntime CRs); `Removed` deletes the controller Deployment,\n64\t  all associated RBAC (ClusterRoles, ClusterRoleBindings, Roles, RoleBindings), the\n65\t  AgentRuntime CRD, the mutating webhook configuration, and namespace-scoped resources\n66\t  in `redhat-ods-applications`.\n67\t- Resolve and document cross-namespace cleanup semantics: what happens to user-created\n68\t  AgentRuntime CRs in other namespaces when the component is disabled (CRD deletion\n69\t  garbage-collects all CRs cluster-wide; the design decision on explicit cross-namespace\n70\t  handling is recorded and tested).\n71\t- Integrate kustomize manifests pulled from the midstream fork at pinned commits into\n72\t  `prefetched-manifests/kagenti-operator/`, with RHOAI-specific overlays for namespace,\n73\t  image references, and RBAC adjustments.\n74\t\n75\t## Acceptance Criteria\n76\t\n77\t- Given a fresh RHOAI deployment with the kagenti-operator component set to\n78\t  `managementState: Managed`, when the DSC controller reconciles, the kagenti-operator\n79\t  Deployment is created in `redhat-ods-applications` with the Konflux-built image and\n80\t  becomes Ready.\n81\t- Given the component changed from `Managed` to `Removed`, when the controller\n82\t  reconciles, all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs including\n83\t  `agentruntimes.agent.kagenti.dev`, webhook configuration) are deleted from the\n84\t  cluster.\n85\t- Given the component is `Managed`, when a user creates an AgentRuntime CR referencing\n86\t  an existing Deployment, the operator applies the `kagenti.io/type: agent` label to\n87\t  the target workload (end-to-end validation of the integrated operator).\n88\t- A Konflux-built image digest for kagenti-operator (and the AuthBridge proxy sidecar)\n89\t  is available and wired into the rendered manifests — configuration reference, filled\n90\t  at execution time.\n91\t- The build pipeline for the onboarded component is green (the Konflux pipeline gate\n92\t  for this integration).\n93\t- Cleanup is tested with resources in multiple namespaces; no orphaned AgentRuntime\n94\t  CRs or webhook configurations persist after disable.\n95\t- Rollback/disable safety: setting the component back to `Removed` fully reverts the\n96\t  cluster to its pre-enable state.\n97\t\n98\t## HLR Traceability\n99\t\n100\t- P0: Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR following the standard\n101\t  component controller pattern — lifecycle enforcement half (RFE acceptance criterion).\n102\t- P0: Full resource cleanup when disabled (RFE acceptance criterion).\n103\t- P0: Tech Preview maturity with explicit opt-in, disabled by default in DSC —\n104\t  enforced by the lifecycle (RFE acceptance criterion).\n105\t- Covers strategy acceptance criteria 1, 2, and 3.\n106\t\n107\t## Risks and Open Questions (in-scope)\n108\t\n109\t- DSC component cleanup leaving orphaned resources — mitigated by an explicit finalizer\n110\t  enumerating owned resources (strategy risk table).\n111\t- kagenti-operator running alongside other platform operators in\n112\t  `redhat-ods-applications` without RBAC conflicts — validated as part of this work\n113\t  (strategy assumption).\n114\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f648cd401ef5cc9","agent_id":"af9f81e901d4d4be6","session_id":"7408e02f-2a40-4c49-b134-f5e8ed6e24cb","uuid":"b88daa9e-8482-426a-8b22-adfc8f17b654","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:44:00.417Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-869b0a989dd1b30e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
