{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84e092ef4a59e764","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E014\n3\ttitle: OTEL trace sink integration for agent workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Model and Agent Observability\n6\tteam: Kagenti\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E004\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E015\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: remove\n17\t  fallback_approach: If the OTEL trace sink MUST stays out of Tech Preview scope,\n18\t    it remains tracked with the parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) and ARC observability work,\n19\t    and this epic is removed.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 0\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n24\t  existing_foundation: 0\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: -1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 0\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: Low\n33\tai_implementability_score: -1\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# OTEL trace sink integration for agent workloads\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tConditional epic, active only if the OTEL trace sink scope resolution pulls the parent\n41\tRFE's OTEL trace sink MUST into this strategy's Tech Preview scope. Delivers the\n42\tminimal OTEL trace sink integration for the kagenti operator, following the\n43\tupstream-first policy: significant changes are contributed to the `kagenti/*`\n44\trepositories first and then pulled into the `opendatahub-io/*` midstream forks before\n45\tbeing packaged into the platform component. The midstream pull extends the component's\n46\trendered manifests, so this epic follows the platform controller and manifest\n47\tintegration work. The DSC component configuration surface that points the trace sink\n48\tat the platform telemetry infrastructure is rhods-operator work owned by the Platform /\n49\tODH Operator team and is covered by a separate conditional epic.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Upstream-first changes to the kagenti operator to support OTEL trace sink\n54\t  configuration, shaped by the minimal integration definition produced by the scope\n55\t  resolution.\n56\t- Midstream pull of the accepted upstream changes into the opendatahub-io forks and\n57\t  into the component's rendered manifests.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- The minimal integration shape defined by the scope resolution is implemented\n62\t  upstream-first (changes accepted in `kagenti/*` before midstream pull).\n63\t- The midstream fork and the component manifests carry the integration.\n64\t- Agent trace data reaches the configured trace sink when the component is `Managed`.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- No existing HLR; this epic materializes the parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) OTEL trace\n69\t  sink MUST if it is affirmed into scope.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f648cd401ef5cc9","agent_id":"af9f81e901d4d4be6","session_id":"7408e02f-2a40-4c49-b134-f5e8ed6e24cb","uuid":"dd18d798-4ae0-4bf5-a58a-68fa632b1715","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:44:03.119Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84e092ef4a59e764","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
